he sample means, ${\\mu }_{1}$ and ${\\mu }_{2}$ are the population means, ${\\sigma }_{1}^{2}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}^{2}$ are the population variances,  ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are the sample sizes,\n\n- $P(Z>{z}_{\\alpha /2})=\\frac{\\alpha }{2}$ and $Z∼N(0,1).$\n\nNow, to construct the confidence interval, we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1.** Find the point estimate:\n\n$$\n{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}-{\\overset{―}{x}}_{2}=31-37=-6\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the margin of error. Since we are interested in finding a $90%$ confidence interval, we have \n\n$$\n\\alpha =1-0.9=0.1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\alpha }{2}=0.05.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $P(Z>1.645)=0.05.$ As a result, \n\n$$\n{z}_{\\alpha /2}={z}_{0.05}=1.645.\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the margin of error:\n\n$$\nE=1.645\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{{5}^{2}}{98}+\\frac{{3}^{2}}{63}}≈1.038\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** Construct the $90%$ confidence interval for the difference between the population means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -6\\pm 1.038\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500340 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172106 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21507a23-f729-56aa-8e9c-66eb5823a2d8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Confidence Intervals Given Two Large Samples"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0409437b-a2c5-53b2-928b-acf3d1eb2629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\pm 1.676" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499658} {:answer/id #uuid "65526a15-276a-5615-b04f-62469c607d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\pm 1.637" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499851} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8c0ca1-5962-5403-b6b1-c4dbeb55c5e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\pm 2.367" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499931} {:answer/id #uuid "c70e8092-9342-5f79-92c0-102cf831a41b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :an